  "preamble": "Retraction of the voiceless velar stop [k] to the uvular [q] next to back vowels. In Selkup, Proto-Samoyedic *k before back vowels regularly became q (*kålä 'fish' > Taz Selkup qē̮li̮), while it palatalized before front vowels; Tundra Nenets instead has χ and Nganasan keeps k. In Eastern (Surgut) Khanty, Proto-Khanty *k in back-vowel words is likewise uvular q (ӄуԓ [quːɬ] 'fish'), where Northern Khanty has χ. In North Dravidian, Proto-Dravidian *k was retracted to *q before vowels other than *i; Malto keeps q (*kaṇ 'eye' > qanu), while Kurukh and Brahui spirantized it to x.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Retraction, Uvularization",
